  "worked_solution": "Let's examine each of the equations in turn.\n\n- The equation ${x}_{1}^{2}=6$ defines a non-empty set. It represents two parallel lines, ${x}_{1}=-\\sqrt{6}$ and ${x}_{1}=\\sqrt{6}.$\n\n- The equation ${x}_{1}^{2}+\\frac{{x}_{2}^{2}}{5}=-1$ defines an empty set. Notice that the left-hand side is non-negative for all ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2},$ while the right-hand side is negative.\n\n- The equation ${x}_{2}^{2}=-7$ defines an empty set. Notice that the left-hand side is non-negative for all ${x}_{2},$ while the right-hand side is negative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"",
